{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Why do you rival:</b> You lofty mountains, humble yourselves. And this meaning is joined until 'though you lie down among the sheepfolds.' And the sense: Let no mountain of Bashan humble itself, for you are a mountain that the angels desired to dwell upon — even the Shekhinah will dwell there."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 68, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:09.111238860Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}